      "final_message": "Both changes are applied. Here's the summary:\n\n**Bug:** When a check received a `/start` ping, it went down after only `last_start + grace` instead of `last_start + timeout + grace`. With period=1hr and grace=1hr, if a `/start` ping arrived 10 minutes after the last success ping, the check would go down at 70 minutes instead of the expected 2 hours.\n\n**Two fixes in `hc/api/models.py`:**\n\n1. **`get_grace_start()` line 335:** Changed `min(result, self.last_start)` to `min(result, self.last_start + self.timeout)` \u2014 this controls `alert_after` (when `sendalerts` picks up the check).\n\n2. **`get_status()` line 360:** Changed `self.last_start + self.grace` to `self.last_start + self.timeout + self.grace` \u2014 this controls the actual status calculation when `sendalerts` evaluates the check.\n\nBoth paths now consistently wait for `timeout + grace` from the start time before marking the check as down, matching the user's expectation that period + grace = total wait time.",
